Aether: adblock and settings polish

Filter-list update modes, design-switch removal from the new page, per-list update status, subhead hierarchy.

Squashed from 4 units:

  [core/171-list-update-modes.patch]
  Aether: filter-list update modes (manual/automatic/scheduled)
  
  The auto-update checkbox becomes a three-way cadence like the
  fingerprint profiles: manual never checks on its own, automatic checks
  at startup, scheduled additionally re-checks while open. One-time
  migration carries the old checkbox into Automatic.
  
  Gates: gate171 static asserts, series applies from base, tree diff 0/0/0,
  TODO OK, build+package exit 0, version string, smoke clean.
  Note (revert per direction: stock about:preferences UI dropped, only the new about:aethersettings UI is kept).
  
  [core/174-no-design-switch.patch]
  Aether: interface design switch removed from the new settings
  
  Per direction only the new about:aethersettings is kept: the Interface
  design row (Aether/Firefox radios) plus its restart banner leave the
  Appearance section, with their script wiring (getDesign/applyDesign,
  restart banner sync, restart button) and orphaned .ds/.restart CSS.
  The aether.ui.design pref stays pinned at its "aether" default as a
  hidden fallback for the hamburger/shields/trust gates until
  about:preferences is deleted outright; the stock-side radios die with it.
  
  [core/175-list-update-status.patch]
  Aether: filter-list rows report version and update result
  
  Pressing Update on a list now says what happened: the fetched version
  plus "Updated just now" when it moved, or "Already up to date" when
  the download matches what was stored. Built-in rows carry a persistent
  version badge; custom rows extend their url/version line; the footer
  "Update now" answers the same way ("Updated", "Already up to date",
  "Updated - N failed") and refreshes every visible row so rows agree
  with it. The engine reports per-key `changed` from both update entry
  points and merges fetched versions into the live map so status reads
  stay fresh without waiting for a lazy rebuild.
  
  [core/176-subhead-hierarchy.patch]
  Aether: list-vendor subheads read as labels, not items
  
  Inside a filter category, vendor subheads ("AdGuard/uBO - Cookie
  Notices") wore full row styling with no toggle, reading as broken
  items. They are muted small-caps labels now, and the lists under them
  indent one more level past the label, so the hierarchy scans at a
  glance. Rows without a subhead stay flush under their category head.
